    "representation": "Each nonempty archived text line with at least one recognized rune defines one row. Include headings. Remove non-alphabet characters; ignore rows with no recognized runes. No corrections or decryption. LP2-50 contributes zero eligible rows.",
    "procedure": "Total number of rows whose prime-value sum is prime, has a prime base-ten decimal reversal, and differs from its reversal. One global statistic; per-page counts are descriptive only. Independently permute the full rune multiset within each page, then partition it using that page’s original row lengths. Preserve page counts and every row length, not words or per-row counts.",
    "parameters": "594 eligible rows; 56 declared pages, 55 with runic rows; 999 full-dataset trials; seed 330133; greater-than-or-equal upper tail; plus-one Monte Carlo correction; alpha 0.05.",
    "exclusions": "Prime palindromes, prime ordinals, decoded text, arbitrary regions, changed spellings, other bases or boundaries and page-specific significance claims."
  },
  "outcome": "not-supported",
  "finding": "41 emirp-valued rows; 539/999 shuffled totals meet or exceed 41, giving corrected upper-tail p=0.540. All baseline prime-count vectors reproduce.",
  "limitations": "Global row-boundary count only. No evidence of excess under this model does not exclude deliberate individual sums or establish randomness. Uses the same shuffles as the prime baseline, not independent evidence. Human review pending.",
  "next_steps": "Declare other boundaries, numeral bases or selected-region rules separately. Account for selection when choosing among alternative properties.",
